.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH archive 1  "archive " 
.SH NAME
archive \- Archive one or more items — "closed and put away". Cascades DOWN: each root and its whole `belongs_to` subtree are archived, but only when the root is closed and every descendant is closed (already\-archived counts as closed). Atomic per root, independent between roots; the result reports each root\*(Aqs outcome plus the full list of ids actually archived (incl. cascaded). Archiving is reversible — see `unarchive`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBarchive\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIIDS\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Archive one or more items — "closed and put away". Cascades DOWN: each root and its whole `belongs_to` subtree are archived, but only when the root is closed and every descendant is closed (already\-archived counts as closed). Atomic per root, independent between roots; the result reports each root\*(Aqs outcome plus the full list of ids actually archived (incl. cascaded). Archiving is reversible — see `unarchive`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIIDS\fR>
Item ids to archive (each a cascade root). At least one is required
